        "name": "Gracanica Monastery and Gazimestan",
        "description": "A fourteenth-century Serbian Orthodox monastery and a medieval battlefield memorial near Pristina.",
        "details": "Gracanica is a UNESCO-listed monastery with Byzantine-style frescoes and an enclave of Serbs around it. Gazimestan is a memorial on the Kosovo Polje plain. Dress modestly, and go with a guide who can explain the history. Both are a short drive from the capital.",
        "interests": [
